<h3>My Component</h3>

<p id="e7ab04f1-1f21-4c0c-aabd-078030b87b42" class=""><strong>Exercise</strong>: In the exercises folder, create a file <code>myComponent.bx</code> which is a class. In component.bxm, make a form that accepts 3 numbers. Create a form on this page which accepts 3 inputs.  When the form is submitted, send the three numbers to a function in myComponent.bx and display the product of the three numbers on the page.</p><br>

<bx:set myComponent = createObject("myComponent") />

<bx:output>

    <form action="#cgi.SCRIPT_NAME#?#cgi.QUERY_STRING#" method="post">

        <p>
            <label for="numone">First number: </label>
            <input id="numone" name="numone" value="0">
        </p>
        <p>
            <label for="numtwo">Second number: </label>
            <input id="numtwo" name="numtwo" value="0">
        </p>
        <p>
            <label for="numthree">Second number: </label>
            <input id="numthree" name="numthree" value="0">
        </p>

        <p>
            <input type="submit" value="Multiply">
        </p>

    </form>

    Result:
    <b>
        #myComponent.multiplyTheNumbers(numone,numtwo,numthree)#
    </b>

</bx:output>